WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:00.020 --> 00:05.110
[This series contains scenes of violence, self-harm, and potential triggers.]

3
00:04.390 --> 00:05.460
What are you doing?

4
00:05.630 --> 00:06.690
Where's Sungwoo?

5
00:06.840 --> 00:07.890
He went home.

6
00:10.180 --> 00:12.110
-What's wrong? -I don't like this.

7
01:00.500 --> 01:02.640
[CEO: Lee Won]

8
01:07.040 --> 01:10.350
[Medical Expense Settlement Statement/Receipt]

9
01:22.170 --> 01:25.300
It seems you can't change your bad habit of stealing.

10
01:29.940 --> 01:33.870
You don't really think a few sheets of music can keep Lee Hanyul, do you?

11
01:34.090 --> 01:35.470
Tell me about it.

12
01:35.789 --> 01:38.050
I didn't expect it to be this easy either.

13
01:38.479 --> 01:42.009
I just gave him a sheet of music, and he left with me immediately.

14
01:42.880 --> 01:44.420
You must be heartbroken.

15
01:46.820 --> 01:48.970
Everyone has a past.

16
01:49.340 --> 01:51.940
But he's by my side now.

17
01:52.940 --> 01:54.890
Is it really just the past?

18
01:56.920 --> 01:58.220
You...

19
02:00.410 --> 02:02.840
Your impatience is the problem.

20
02:04.660 --> 02:06.360
Going as far as breaking into my locker to steal the music—

21
02:06.360 --> 02:08.030
It's not really your place to say that, is it?

22
02:08.030 --> 02:11.160
It's all because you kept threatening him for no reason.

23
02:11.920 --> 02:13.500
I wasn't threatening him.

24
02:15.540 --> 02:18.390
I was just helping him come back to me faster.

25
02:24.010 --> 02:26.070
Didn't you come here to get this back?

26
02:28.870 --> 02:30.579
Ah, that?

27
02:31.410 --> 02:33.640
This method won't last long anyway.

28
02:46.130 --> 02:48.650
He clearly has a backup plan.

29
02:54.090 --> 03:00.750
[Some scenes were created with AI.]

30
03:02.870 --> 03:06.700
[Adapted from the webtoon "The Sound of Sugar Cubes" by Kim Tak]

31
03:06.700 --> 03:09.460
[Screenwriter: So-on (JD)]

32
03:09.460 --> 03:12.390
[Director: Yoon Jinyoung]

33
03:28.870 --> 03:30.480
[Yoo Dohyun]

34
03:30.490 --> 03:32.120
[Cho Chanhyeon]

35
03:32.120 --> 03:33.750
[Ko Gyeol]

36
03:35.380 --> 03:38.700
[The Sound of Sugar Cubes]

37
03:45.180 --> 03:46.690
Oh, seriously.

38
03:48.390 --> 03:50.390
What are you dissatisfied with now?

39
03:54.150 --> 03:56.560
Did... Did something happen?

40
03:56.570 --> 03:59.980
This guy hasn't been listening to me for a while.

41
04:00.140 --> 04:02.380
I didn't want to hit it...

42
04:02.820 --> 04:03.660
Damn it.

43
04:03.830 --> 04:05.050
Boomboom!

44
04:05.210 --> 04:06.620
Wake up!

45
04:07.550 --> 04:10.210
How can a machine like you change just like that?

46
04:10.960 --> 04:12.380
You've changed.

47
04:12.550 --> 04:13.750
I'm sorry, Boomboom.

48
04:13.860 --> 04:15.430
I hit you too hard.

49
04:16.540 --> 04:18.720
It probably broke because it's been used for too long.

50
04:18.720 --> 04:20.959
It is quite old.

51
04:21.180 --> 04:24.110
But I'm not ready to let it go yet.

52
04:24.310 --> 04:26.920
I'm not mentally prepared, my Boomboom.

53
04:27.050 --> 04:29.370
Is this... very expensive?

54
04:29.490 --> 04:32.400
Boomboom... is worth this much.

55
04:32.970 --> 04:33.900
Three million?

56
04:34.120 --> 04:36.250
No, I mean Boomboom is worth this much.

57
04:36.409 --> 04:37.540
Thirty million?

58
04:37.659 --> 04:38.760
Yeah.

59
04:40.300 --> 04:43.650
I'm sorry I made you unable to take other jobs.

60
04:44.110 --> 04:46.730
What, are you planning to buy me a new set?

61
04:48.850 --> 04:49.900
No.

62
04:49.900 --> 04:51.370
Don't listen.

63
04:51.520 --> 04:53.490
Boomboom, don't listen.

64
04:56.050 --> 04:57.060
I'm sorry.

65
04:59.310 --> 05:00.470
Boomboom...

66
05:02.330 --> 05:03.550
Hello?

67
05:04.120 --> 05:05.930
Is this Mr. Lee Hanyul?

68
05:06.070 --> 05:09.400
This is the Talent Development Team at Dawn Entertainment.

69
05:09.780 --> 05:11.710
Look into my eyes.

70
05:12.560 --> 05:14.420
Don't cry, Boomboom.

71
05:14.990 --> 05:16.690
Dawn Entertainment?

72
05:21.030 --> 05:22.170
Boomboom...

73
05:22.870 --> 05:23.780
I'm sorry...

74
05:24.050 --> 05:27.060
[Producer: Michelo]

75
05:43.440 --> 05:46.630
Sorry, my meeting ended a bit late.

76
05:46.790 --> 05:47.990
It's fine.

77
05:49.500 --> 05:50.740
Have a seat.

78
05:54.600 --> 05:55.820
I am...

79
05:56.870 --> 05:59.030
Producer Michelo.

80
06:00.160 --> 06:02.430
My name is Lee Hanyul.

81
06:02.610 --> 06:04.410
What did you want to see me about?

82
06:06.170 --> 06:07.900
Have you signed with an agency?

83
06:07.950 --> 06:09.350
An agency?

84
06:10.220 --> 06:12.540
I haven't signed... with any.

85
06:12.770 --> 06:14.050
What about a manager?

86
06:14.740 --> 06:16.650
I don't have a manager either.

87
06:17.170 --> 06:18.320
Is that so?

88
06:20.380 --> 06:23.120
I heard our Team Leader Ko

89
06:23.270 --> 06:26.250
left you a business card at the Sandol Village festival.

90
06:26.250 --> 06:27.790
You never contacted us,

91
06:27.920 --> 06:31.990
but recently, someone related to you called us.

92
06:32.210 --> 06:33.870
Someone related to me?

93
06:34.570 --> 06:36.020
Who could it be...

94
06:37.490 --> 06:39.330
I'm not too sure who that could be,

95
06:39.330 --> 06:41.330
but I do have a teacher.

96
06:41.780 --> 06:42.900
A teacher?

97
06:43.170 --> 06:44.100
Yes.

98
06:44.220 --> 06:47.159
His name is Mr. Pan. He gives me vocal lessons.

99
06:48.540 --> 06:49.710
Pan?

100
06:49.860 --> 06:51.880
Yes. Do you know him?

101
07:01.450 --> 07:03.980
Let's not go around in circles.

102
07:04.120 --> 07:05.850
Sign with our agency.

103
07:06.820 --> 07:09.000
I've seen your videos.

104
07:09.130 --> 07:10.600
I'll help you debut.

105
07:10.840 --> 07:13.060
Also, whatever conditions you want,

106
07:13.200 --> 07:14.510
I can satisfy them.

107
07:14.640 --> 07:16.470
Is there anything you want?

108
07:23.700 --> 07:26.010
Boomboom... is worth this much.

109
07:26.100 --> 07:27.080
Three million?

110
07:27.230 --> 07:29.360
No, I mean Boomboom is worth this much.

111
07:29.450 --> 07:30.690
Thirty million?

112
07:31.670 --> 07:34.630
I'd like to get the signing bonus first.

113
07:35.000 --> 07:35.930
Okay.

114
07:37.430 --> 07:39.760
Also, there's a song I really want to sing.

115
07:39.820 --> 07:41.560
A song you really want to sing?

116
07:41.970 --> 07:43.110
Yes.

117
07:43.270 --> 07:45.740
I want to debut with this song.

118
07:46.270 --> 07:47.490
Sure.

119
07:47.650 --> 07:49.850
We can consider this later.

120
08:01.880 --> 08:05.900
Then let's release a remake album of old songs first.

121
08:06.090 --> 08:09.230
We'll start recording tomorrow.

122
08:09.390 --> 08:11.210
Tomorrow? That fast?

123
08:11.380 --> 08:12.520
What's wrong?

124
08:12.680 --> 08:16.320
I'm sure that teacher must've trained you well.

125
08:16.670 --> 08:17.710
Ah...

126
08:20.640 --> 08:21.830
Sign it.

127
08:24.550 --> 08:26.520
Right... Right now?

128
08:32.570 --> 08:35.720
[Article 5: Breach of Artist Obligations and Test Content Article 6: Prohibition of Using External Songs and Leakage of Sound Sources Article 7: Profit Distribution and Settlement]

129
08:35.330 --> 08:38.130
The signing bonus can be transferred to you today.

130
08:40.950 --> 08:43.669
One, two, three, four...

131
08:44.169 --> 08:45.370
One hundred million?

132
08:45.410 --> 08:47.890
What, is it not enough?

133
08:48.150 --> 08:49.590
No.

134
08:56.280 --> 08:58.280
The sooner the better.

135
08:58.410 --> 09:00.740
That way you can debut as soon as possible.

136
09:01.310 --> 09:03.770
But this fast is still a bit...

137
09:04.350 --> 09:05.540
Ah.

138
09:05.970 --> 09:08.160
You just asked me if I knew Pan, right?

139
09:08.450 --> 09:09.600
Yes.

140
09:09.960 --> 09:11.370
He's my friend.

141
09:11.530 --> 09:13.080
An old friend of many years.

142
09:13.650 --> 09:15.070
Really?

143
09:15.940 --> 09:19.030
That's why I proposed to sign as soon as possible.

144
09:19.160 --> 09:22.830
His beloved student must have reliable skills.

145
09:29.270 --> 09:32.570
I have another appointment next.

146
09:32.700 --> 09:35.240
If you don't want to sign, you don't have to.

147
09:35.890 --> 09:37.210
I'll sign.

148
09:55.450 --> 09:56.550
Good.

149
09:57.120 --> 09:58.910
See you at the recording tomorrow.

150
09:58.910 --> 09:59.730
Okay.

151
09:59.950 --> 10:00.850
Ah.

152
10:01.320 --> 10:04.470
If it's convenient, you can invite your teacher along.

153
10:05.420 --> 10:07.620
It would give me a rare chance to see him.

154
10:08.450 --> 10:09.710
Thank you.

155
10:11.090 --> 10:12.370
Thank you!

156
10:24.230 --> 10:25.620
Where is Lee Hanyul?

157
10:26.340 --> 10:27.240
I don't know.

158
10:27.370 --> 10:29.170
I saw him answer a call and go out.

159
10:29.710 --> 10:30.550
A call?

160
10:30.820 --> 10:32.460
Dusk...

161
10:32.590 --> 10:34.520
Dusk Entertainment or something.

162
10:34.900 --> 10:36.860
There's no such entertainment company.

163
10:36.860 --> 10:38.940
Why would an entertainment company look for him?

164
10:38.940 --> 10:42.130
I don't know. It's probably a phishing scam.

165
10:52.770 --> 10:53.810
What...

166
10:55.670 --> 10:57.180
-Hey! -Help me.

167
10:57.720 --> 10:58.810
Hey, what...

168
11:02.900 --> 11:04.300
What is this?

169
11:04.870 --> 11:06.070
Gah!

170
11:06.180 --> 11:07.560
Could... Could this be?

171
11:08.910 --> 11:11.030
This is a gift to thank you, Mr. Pan.

172
11:13.320 --> 11:16.200
You're not the victim of a phishing scam, but you scammed someone else instead?

173
11:16.200 --> 11:17.880
It's not like that.

174
11:21.520 --> 11:22.910
You brat.

175
11:27.100 --> 11:28.670
Boomboom...

176
11:28.810 --> 11:30.200
My Boomboom...

177
11:36.460 --> 11:37.610
So...

178
11:38.810 --> 11:41.140
Where did you get such a large sum of money?

179
11:41.570 --> 11:42.700
It's a secret.

180
11:44.810 --> 11:45.860
Hey.

181
11:46.760 --> 11:48.790
Do you know how expensive this thing is?

182
11:48.790 --> 11:51.370
I know. I bought it.

183
11:54.230 --> 11:55.690
Hehe.

184
11:55.880 --> 11:57.420
You are the new Boomboom.

185
11:57.600 --> 11:58.780
New Boomboom.

186
12:00.350 --> 12:03.320
I want to debut as soon as possible to pay off the favors I owe,

187
12:03.320 --> 12:04.890
to pay off what I owe Mr. Pan.

188
12:05.220 --> 12:07.700
Boomboom, hehe.

189
12:14.260 --> 12:15.750
And pay off what I owe you.

190
12:17.830 --> 12:20.350
I'll be able to sing your songs soon too.

191
12:32.650 --> 12:33.750
Don't be nervous.

192
12:33.980 --> 12:35.840
Just sing with a relaxed mind.

193
12:36.130 --> 12:37.190
Okay.

194
12:38.830 --> 12:39.920
Drink this.

195
12:40.370 --> 12:41.580
Thank you.

196
13:07.420 --> 13:08.630
Can you hear me?

197
13:11.850 --> 13:14.810
Give me a signal when you're ready.

198
13:24.680 --> 13:25.730
Okay.

199
13:25.920 --> 13:27.180
Here it comes.

200
13:27.340 --> 13:29.020
Play the MR.

201
14:18.830 --> 14:23.350
How could you sign the contract knowing you had a problem with your voice?

202
14:27.470 --> 14:30.450
You have an obligation to seriously cooperate with the company for the designated tests.

203
14:30.450 --> 14:33.170
If the project is halted due to the signing party's own reasons,

204
14:33.170 --> 14:35.960
the company has the right to recover the initial investment and losses,

205
14:35.960 --> 14:39.180
and all expenses must be fully refunded to the agency.

206
14:36.910 --> 14:39.150
[Must be fully refunded to the agency.]

207
14:42.450 --> 14:43.820
Recording engineers,

208
14:43.950 --> 14:44.950
the manpower responsible for you,

209
14:44.950 --> 14:46.310
and preparations—

210
14:46.440 --> 14:48.750
all of these cost money.

211
14:55.320 --> 14:58.690
Now, because you breached the contract, both parties are terminating it.

212
14:58.690 --> 15:00.170
[Indictment]

213
14:58.990 --> 15:00.050
As for the penalty,

214
15:00.080 --> 15:02.820
I will thoroughly discuss it with the legal team

215
15:03.100 --> 15:04.790
and let you know later.

216
15:05.390 --> 15:06.480
Hanyul!

217
15:11.890 --> 15:15.920
Wow, friend, long time no see.

218
15:18.250 --> 15:20.060
[Indictment]

219
15:24.680 --> 15:25.400
Bastard...

220
15:25.550 --> 15:26.600
Stop!

221
15:29.440 --> 15:31.280
Take Hanyul away.

222
15:31.700 --> 15:33.140
This is my problem.

223
15:37.880 --> 15:38.970
Let's go.

224
15:47.370 --> 15:48.170
How did you...

225
15:48.240 --> 15:49.810
You want to ask why we knew?

226
15:50.140 --> 15:52.000
It's because you act too weirdly.

227
15:54.650 --> 15:55.980
Don't speak.

228
15:58.510 --> 16:00.210
Thankfully we managed to treat it soon enough,

229
16:00.210 --> 16:03.040
so the vocal cords are not completely damaged.

230
16:03.220 --> 16:04.410
As long as he doesn't overuse his voice,

231
16:04.410 --> 16:05.610
he will recover soon.

232
16:05.770 --> 16:06.960
Okay, thank you.

233
16:07.120 --> 16:07.920
Sure.

234
16:15.450 --> 16:17.320
Did he give you anything?

235
16:21.930 --> 16:23.190
Pan

236
16:23.340 --> 16:26.200
used to be the lead singer of a very popular group...

237
16:28.000 --> 16:30.980
in the same group as Michelo.

238
16:48.860 --> 16:50.040
What?

239
16:50.840 --> 16:52.990
Are you going to kneel before me?

240
17:03.060 --> 17:04.609
What's going on?

241
17:05.210 --> 17:07.470
Pan is past his prime.

242
17:10.109 --> 17:12.700
Please don't touch Hanyul.

243
17:13.800 --> 17:17.560
The contract and the penalty—

244
17:18.530 --> 17:20.560
let's just pretend it never happened.

245
17:20.560 --> 17:22.660
I'm begging you as a friend.

246
17:28.560 --> 17:31.650
Do you think begging me will solve it?

247
17:37.400 --> 17:41.540
Do you know why I hate you so much?

248
17:45.020 --> 17:48.240
You always look at me with pity.

249
17:50.230 --> 17:56.410
I tried my best just to stand by your side in this life.

250
17:56.970 --> 17:59.860
But you never saw me as a rival.

251
18:01.480 --> 18:04.170
I thought we were on the same team.

252
18:05.410 --> 18:07.580
That's exactly it!

253
18:07.870 --> 18:10.510
That's the most disgusting part. Damn it.

254
18:10.780 --> 18:13.430
Hey, I...

255
18:13.510 --> 18:15.920
did everything I could to beat you.

256
18:16.050 --> 18:18.020
But you didn't even consider me a rival.

257
18:18.020 --> 18:21.950
You just thought of me as your useless sidekick, right?

258
18:25.640 --> 18:27.120
The contract?

259
18:28.000 --> 18:29.400
Fine.

260
18:29.890 --> 18:31.840
Let's pretend it never happened.

261
18:36.920 --> 18:38.500
But...

262
18:57.350 --> 18:59.840
What's going on?

263
18:59.960 --> 19:02.080
Were you waiting for me?

264
19:02.710 --> 19:04.010
Shh.

265
19:04.550 --> 19:06.300
Don't say anything.

266
19:06.440 --> 19:08.320
You can't speak anyway.

267
19:08.540 --> 19:09.460
Don't worry, kid.

268
19:09.460 --> 19:12.190
I've taken care of everything.

269
19:17.700 --> 19:18.680
What is this?

270
19:21.930 --> 19:26.490
I wanted to help you and Lee Won.

271
19:22.140 --> 19:34.380
[I wanted to help you and Lee Won. But I didn't even discuss it with you, and foolishly signed the contract. I feel so stupid.]

272
19:26.610 --> 19:27.960
But I didn't even discuss it with you,

273
19:27.960 --> 19:30.830
and foolishly signed the contract.

274
19:30.940 --> 19:32.710
I feel so stupid.

275
19:35.640 --> 19:41.910
[It's my fault you had to go through such a terrible thing. I messed everything up. You worked so hard for me, and it's all my fault. I'm sorry, I'm really sorry.]

276
19:44.300 --> 19:45.310
Oh, you brat.

277
19:45.450 --> 19:47.490
What did you do wrong?

278
19:47.600 --> 19:50.090
It's just old geezers trying to satisfy their own desires.

279
19:50.090 --> 19:53.030
Why are you putting yourself down, brat?

280
19:53.130 --> 19:54.600
It's okay, kid.

281
19:55.510 --> 19:56.580
Hey.

282
19:57.210 --> 20:00.320
Speaking of, you type really fast.

283
20:01.100 --> 20:02.360
You're quite capable.

284
20:02.620 --> 20:04.730
You don't even need to speak.

285
20:08.740 --> 20:10.460
I'm taking him away today.

286
20:10.770 --> 20:12.370
Go out first.

287
20:15.750 --> 20:16.940
Hey.

288
20:17.690 --> 20:21.740
The dangerous one for Hanyul isn't Michelo,

289
20:21.860 --> 20:23.900
but you.

290
20:24.190 --> 20:25.370
Are you okay?

291
20:26.530 --> 20:27.670
What do you mean?

292
20:27.900 --> 20:29.620
Nothing happened.

293
20:30.160 --> 20:31.880
What exactly happened?

294
20:34.380 --> 20:39.110
Give me the copyrights to all the songs under your name.

295
20:39.670 --> 20:40.980
Also,

296
20:41.220 --> 20:43.950
whatever songs you write in the future

297
20:44.080 --> 20:49.300
must be registered under my name.

298
20:51.020 --> 20:52.470
You...

299
20:53.360 --> 20:56.160
will be my ghostwriter for the rest of your life.

300
20:58.900 --> 21:00.080
Okay.

301
21:01.220 --> 21:03.050
Let's do that, friend.

302
21:10.790 --> 21:14.070
Maybe she still thinks I'm a genius.

303
21:14.370 --> 21:16.500
That I just need to write songs for her.

304
21:17.270 --> 21:19.810
We're all friends. We've cleared things up.

305
21:20.060 --> 21:23.170
Gosh, she really liked me.

306
21:23.860 --> 21:25.790
But it's a pity.

307
21:26.200 --> 21:29.340
I was planning to make a fortune off Hanyul's good voice.

308
21:29.540 --> 21:30.930
Seriously.

309
21:31.430 --> 21:32.360
Tsk.

310
21:32.650 --> 21:33.770
What's wrong?

311
21:35.620 --> 21:36.690
What...

312
21:36.810 --> 21:38.010
What's your issue?

313
21:45.430 --> 21:46.650
Blow your nose.

314
22:03.210 --> 22:04.330
Here.

315
22:06.260 --> 22:07.460
Done.

316
22:10.310 --> 22:13.240
I look so stupid, right?

317
22:14.030 --> 22:15.860
You're not stupid.

318
22:18.980 --> 22:21.710
I should have killed that woman earlier.

319
22:30.160 --> 22:31.370
Lee Hanyul.

320
22:33.670 --> 22:35.620
Do you still want to sing?

321
22:38.790 --> 22:39.880
There we go.

322
22:40.050 --> 22:41.220
Stop crying.

323
22:41.990 --> 22:43.610
Go wash up and go to sleep.

324
23:05.680 --> 23:06.870
All right.

325
23:13.320 --> 23:14.610
Hanyul.

326
23:19.490 --> 23:21.650
Whether it's in the past or now,

327
23:24.730 --> 23:27.140
you did nothing wrong.

328
23:32.700 --> 23:35.570
So you don't have to run away,

329
23:37.620 --> 23:39.470
and you don't have to cry.

330
23:46.020 --> 23:47.890
Don't cry.

331
23:54.140 --> 23:57.120
When you cry, I don't know what to do.

332
27:10.080 --> 27:13.240
[The Sound of Sugar Cubes]

333
27:13.260 --> 27:14.400
Hey, fire!

334
27:14.540 --> 27:15.930
Fire! Fire!

335
27:16.280 --> 27:17.330
Hmm?

336
27:17.490 --> 27:18.350
I am an idiot.

337
27:18.500 --> 27:20.680
So until your voice goes back to normal,

338
27:20.680 --> 27:22.240
I'll continue to be an idiot.

339
27:22.240 --> 27:23.570
It's finally done—

340
27:23.810 --> 27:25.520
[The Sound of Sugar Cubes]

341
27:23.920 --> 27:25.140
the song I want to give you.

342
27:25.140 --> 27:27.490
Adolph... is gone.

343
27:27.730 --> 27:28.660
What did you say?

344
27:28.660 --> 27:29.650
It's true.

345
27:29.810 --> 27:31.410
I really have been taking care of him.

346
27:31.410 --> 27:33.240
Here, are you satisfied now?

347
27:33.460 --> 27:35.780
Just kill me. I beg you to just kill me!

348
27:39.040 --> 27:40.460
Who are you?
